title: MikroTik REST API: MLAG Peer
agents: mikrotik_rest_api
catalog: hw/network/mikrotik
license: GPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 State of the MLAG (multi-chassis link aggregation) peer connection of a
 MikroTik bridge with an MLAG peer port ({/interface/bridge/monitor},
 {mlag-state} and {mlag-active-role}).

 {connected} is OK. {connecting} means the connection to the peer (ICCP
 over the peer port) is down and is CRIT by default; any other state, for
 example an error text like "peer port not running", is CRIT as well.
 The role of this node (primary/secondary) is shown; optionally an
 expected role can be set, a different role is then WARN (the roles
 change when the primary reboots or fails). Levels via the rule
 {MikroTik REST API: MLAG peer}.

 Special agent {MikroTik RouterOS (mikrotik-rest-api)} in Setup > Agents >
 Other integrations, module "MLAG". Field names follow the MikroTik MLAG
 documentation; not yet verified on MLAG hardware.

 Added in mikrotik-rest-api 1.3.0 by Klaus Paulitsch.

item:
 The name of the bridge.

inventory:
 One service per enabled bridge with an MLAG peer port.
